<PageTitle>Master-detail — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Master-detail" Category="Data Grid" CategoryHref="demo/grid" ControlName="GridControl"
                   Tagline="Pick a row and see what belongs to it: in a second grid, or in a detail row that opens under it."
                   SourcePath="Grid/GridControl.razor.cs;Grid/GridControl.AdvancedFeatures.cs;Grid/GridControlEvents.cs;Grid/SelectionSettings.cs;Grid/GridModels.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            A master-detail screen is two ordinary grids and one event. The master grid raises <code>RowSelected</code> (a
            <code>GridControlEvents</code> callback passed through <code>EventsRef</code>) with the selected row in <code>args.Data</code>;
            the page filters its detail list by that row's key and binds the result to the second grid's <code>DataSource</code>.
            <code>SelectionSettings</code> with <code>SelectionType.Single</code> keeps one master row selected, and
            <code>AutoSelectFirstRow</code> selects the first row as soon as the grid has rows and raises <code>RowSelected</code> for it, so
            the detail fills on arrival. <code>RowSelecting</code> can refuse a move while the detail has unsaved edits; the
            <a href="demo/grid/unsaved-row-lock">Unsaved-row lock</a> page shows that.
        </p>
        <p>
            When the detail is short, one grid will do. A <code>DetailTemplate</code> renders under the row that owns it, behind an arrow
            column the grid adds on the left; the grid keeps track of which rows are open and tells the page through <code>RowExpand</code>
            and <code>RowCollapse</code>. Anything can go in the template. The second example puts a second <code>GridControl</code> there.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="groups" Title="Security groups and their members" RazorCode="@Code.Groups" CSharpCode="@Code.GroupsCs">
            <Description><p>Seven groups on the left, 126 users on the right. Click a group and the right grid shows its members; the Users column of the group row, the member grid's footer and the line under the grids count the same people. The member grid sorts on its own and marks inactive accounts.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="pair">
                    <div>
                        <p class="pane-title">Groups</p>
                        <GridControl TValue="SecurityGroup"
                                     DataSource="@_groups"
                                     Height="300px"
                                     AllowSelection="true"
                                     AutoSelectFirstRow="true"
                                     SelectionSettingsRef="@_singleRow"
                                     EventsRef="@_groupEvents">
                            <GridColumnsBase>
                                <GridColumn Field="@nameof(SecurityGroup.Description)" HeaderText="Group" Width="200px" />
                                <GridColumn Field="@nameof(SecurityGroup.IsAdmin)" HeaderText="Admin" Width="80px" Type="ColumnType.Boolean" />
                                <GridColumn Field="@nameof(SecurityGroup.MemberCount)" HeaderText="Users" Width="80px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" />
                            </GridColumnsBase>
                        </GridControl>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <p class="pane-title">Members of @(_selectedGroup?.Description ?? "…")</p>
                        <GridControl TValue="UserListItem"
                                     DataSource="@_members"
                                     Height="300px"
                                     AllowSorting="true"
                                     ShowRowCountInFooter="true">
                            <GridColumnsBase>
                                <GridColumn Field="@nameof(UserListItem.UserID)" HeaderText="Login" Width="100px" />
                                <GridColumn Field="@nameof(UserListItem.UserName)" HeaderText="Name" Width="150px" />
                                <GridColumn Field="@nameof(UserListItem.Email)" HeaderText="Email" Width="210px" />
                                <GridColumn Field="@nameof(UserListItem.Active)" HeaderText="Active" Width="70px" Type="ColumnType.Boolean" />
                            </GridColumnsBase>
                        </GridControl>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="result">@_members.Count members of @(_selectedGroup?.Description ?? "no group"), @_members.Count(u => !u.Active) inactive.</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="warehouses" Title="Products and their warehouse stock" RazorCode="@Code.Warehouses" CSharpCode="@Code.WarehousesCs" CssCode="@Code.WarehousesCss">
            <Description><p>Fifteen products in one grid. The arrow at the left of a row opens a second grid under it with that product's stock per warehouse; <code>ExpandMode.Single</code> keeps one open at a time. Receive the next shipment or reserve stock inside the detail and the product row above recalculates on hand, available and valuation. The category buttons filter the products; when the filter hides the open product the page closes it with <code>CollapseRow</code>.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <ButtonGroupControl Items="CategoryItems" Values="@(new[] { _category })" ValuesChanged="Filter" Selection="ChoiceSelectionMode.Single" AriaLabel="Category" />
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <GridControl @ref="_grid"
                             TValue="InventoryProduct"
                             DataSource="@Shown"
                             Height="400px"
                             AllowSorting="true"
                             ShowRowCountInFooter="true"
                             ExpandMode="GridExpandMode.Single"
                             RowExpand="Opened"
                             RowCollapse="Closed">
                    <ChildContent>
                        <GridColumnsBase>
                            <GridColumn Field="@nameof(InventoryProduct.SKU)" HeaderText="SKU" Width="100px" />
                            <GridColumn Field="@nameof(InventoryProduct.ProductName)" HeaderText="Product" Width="220px" />
                            <GridColumn Field="@nameof(InventoryProduct.Category)" HeaderText="Category" Width="120px" />
                            <GridColumn Field="@nameof(InventoryProduct.TotalOnHand)" HeaderText="On hand" Width="90px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="#,##0" />
                            <GridColumn Field="@nameof(InventoryProduct.TotalReserved)" HeaderText="Reserved" Width="90px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="#,##0" />
                            <GridColumn Field="@nameof(InventoryProduct.AvailableStock)" HeaderText="Available" Width="90px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right">
                                <Template>
                                    @{ var p = (InventoryProduct)context; }
                                    <span class="@(p.AvailableStock <= 0 ? "out" : p.AvailableStock <= p.ReorderPoint ? "low" : "")">@p.AvailableStock.ToString("#,##0")</span>
                                </Template>
                            </GridColumn>
                            <GridColumn Field="@nameof(InventoryProduct.ReorderPoint)" HeaderText="Reorder at" Width="90px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="#,##0" />
                            <GridColumn Field="@nameof(InventoryProduct.InventoryValuation)" HeaderText="Valuation" Width="110px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="C0" />
                        </GridColumnsBase>
                    </ChildContent>
                    <DetailTemplate Context="product">
                        <div class="detail">
                            <div class="detail-bar">
                                <span>@product.WarehouseDetails.Count warehouses hold @product.TotalOnHand.ToString("#,##0") on hand, @product.TotalReserved.ToString("#,##0") reserved, @product.WarehouseDetails.Sum(w => w.IncomingShipmentQty).ToString("#,##0") incoming.</span>
                                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="() => Receive(product)">Receive next shipment</ButtonControl>
                                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="() => Reserve(product)">Reserve 10</ButtonControl>
                            </div>
                            <GridControl TValue="WarehouseStock" DataSource="@product.WarehouseDetails" AllowSorting="true">
                                <GridColumnsBase>
                                    <GridColumn Field="@nameof(WarehouseStock.WarehouseCode)" HeaderText="Code" Width="80px" />
                                    <GridColumn Field="@nameof(WarehouseStock.WarehouseName)" HeaderText="Warehouse" Width="160px" />
                                    <GridColumn Field="@nameof(WarehouseStock.LocationBin)" HeaderText="Bin" Width="120px" />
                                    <GridColumn Field="@nameof(WarehouseStock.QuantityOnHand)" HeaderText="On hand" Width="85px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="#,##0" />
                                    <GridColumn Field="@nameof(WarehouseStock.ReservedQuantity)" HeaderText="Reserved" Width="85px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="#,##0" />
                                    <GridColumn Field="@nameof(WarehouseStock.AvailableQuantity)" HeaderText="Available" Width="85px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="#,##0" />
                                    <GridColumn Field="@nameof(WarehouseStock.IncomingShipmentQty)" HeaderText="Incoming" Width="85px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="#,##0" />
                                    <GridColumn Field="@nameof(WarehouseStock.NextDeliveryDate)" HeaderText="Next delivery" Width="105px" Type="ColumnType.Date" Format="yyyy-MM-dd" />
                                    <GridColumn Field="@nameof(WarehouseStock.BatchLotNumber)" HeaderText="Lot" Width="120px" />
                                </GridColumnsBase>
                            </GridControl>
                        </div>
                    </DetailTemplate>
                </GridControl>
                <p class="result">@Shown.Count products worth @Shown.Sum(p => p.InventoryValuation).ToString("C0") on hand@(_open is null ? "; no detail open." : $"; {_open.SKU} open.")</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-gridcontrol-selection-parameters" Title="GridControl selection parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Grid.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="GridControl selection parameters" Rows="Vocab.Grid" />
            </DocSection>
